<title>USA: Tellabs wins $4 mln Alberta phone pact.</title>
<headline>Tellabs wins $4 mln Alberta phone pact.</headline>
<dateline>LISLE, Ill. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tellabs Inc said Wednesday that Alberta-based TELUS Corp signed a 10-year agreement for Tellab's SONET-based TITAN 5500 digital cross-connect system.</p>
<p>Initial purchases under the agreement were valued at more than $4 million, Tellabs said.</p>
<p>The TITAN 5500 digital cross-connect system is Tellabs' flagship product in North America and is used by local, long-distance, wireless and alternate service carriers.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
